# Aligned to Angular 22's documented Baseline browser-support definition
# (https://angular.dev/reference/versions#browser-support): the browsers in
# the Baseline "widely available" set AS OF 2026-05-07.
#
# The date is PINNED, not rolling, because Angular 22's definition is itself
# fixed to that date. A bare `baseline widely available` query resolves to
# TODAY's Baseline and therefore drifts further from Angular 22 every day --
# and drifts LOOSER, since newer floors drop older browsers. Measured: the
# rolling query resolved to 125 targets (chrome/edge 121, firefox 122,
# safari/ios_saf 17.2) where the pinned query resolves to 136 (chrome/edge/
# firefox 119, safari/ios_saf 17.0).
#
# browserslist 4.28.7 supports the pinned form natively and resolves it
# through `baseline-browser-mapping`, the same data source behind
# https://web-platform-dx.github.io/supported-browsers/ (includeDownstream=false).
#
# scripts/verify-browserslist.mjs asserts this exact query (R022).
baseline widely available on 2026-05-07
